# Keep every published file LF, whatever editor touches it.
#
# This repository is created and committed from WSL, where everything is already
# LF, and it ships shell scripts — a CRLF in a shebang breaks them on Linux. The
# concrete risk is someone editing through the Windows side (Notepad, Windows VS
# Code) over a \\wsl.localhost path, which introduces CRLF silently. Pinning it
# here makes that impossible rather than merely unlikely.
#
# NOT covered here, and worth knowing: the executable bit. Git has no attribute
# for file mode, so install.sh, uninstall.sh, and scripts/link-deps.sh depend on
# `core.fileMode=true` (true in WSL, frequently false on Windows). After editing
# from the Windows side, confirm with:
#
#     git ls-files -s install.sh      # must print 100755
#
* text=auto eol=lf
